\ cv8b-kinput.4 - the input side made faster (Iteration 54), for the
\ byte-header system with kfast; loaded after cv8b-kfast.4 for designs
\ with the gene kinput. X8 words: the kernel's word gets the body.
\
\ On seed 12's fastest design, REFILL, SCAN, PARSE, SKIP and WORD were
\ 27-36% of the kernel, parse and corpus workloads' dispatches. Most of
\ REFILL's share was its tab loop - ten dispatches a character of every
\ line read - factored out here as TABS>BL, a format-10 opcode with SCAN,
\ SKIP and FILL. Since Iterations 145 and 148 no tab is made a space: SKIP
\ and SCAN take any control character for a space delimiter, and TABS>BL
\ is gone (lab/evolve).


: REFILL8 ( --- f)
\ The kernel's REFILL.
  SOURCE-ID -1 = IF
   0 \ Not refillable for EVALUATE
  ELSE
   SOURCE-ID IF
    SRC @ 256 SOURCE-ID READ-LINE ABORT" Error reading file"
    SWAP #SRC ! 0 >IN !
    \ No tab is made a space (Iterations 145, 148): SKIP and SCAN take control
    \ characters for a space delimiter.
   ELSE
    QUERY #TIB @ #SRC ! 0 >IN ! -1 \ Always successful from terminal.
   THEN
  THEN ;

\ After the tab loop (Iteration 54, attributed again): PARSE's own stack work
\ 9-14% of kernel, parse and corpus; ?STACK's check, run after every word
\ interpreted, calling (ABORT") each time only to skip its message.

: (PARSE) ( addr u c --- a1 len adv )
\ Skip the leading c's, then up to the next c: the string between, and
\ how far >IN moves - to that c and past it, if there was one. PARSE-WORD's
\ work - WORD's; PARSE skips nothing since Iteration 125 - as the kernel does it with SKIP and SCAN.
  ROT DUP >R ROT ROT DUP >R SKIP OVER SWAP R> SCAN
  IF 1 ELSE 0 THEN OVER R> - + >R OVER - R> ;

: PARSE-WORD8 ( c --- addr len )
\ The kernel's PARSE-WORD (PARSE until Iteration 125): the rest of the
\ source from >IN, (PARSE), >IN moved.
  >R SOURCE SWAP >IN @ + SWAP >IN @ - R> (PARSE) >IN +! ;

: ?STACK8 ( --- )
\ The kernel's ?STACK - DEPTH below 0 or above 10000 - as one unsigned
\ compare (DEPTH's logical shift makes an underflow huge), and (ABORT")
\ called only when there is something to say.
  DEPTH 10000 U> IF -1 ABORT" Stack error" THEN ;
